.TH UNGETC 3S
.SH NAME
ungetc \- push character back into input stream
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
.B "#include <stdio.h>"
.sp
.B "ungetc(c, stream)"
.B "FILE *stream;"
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B ungetc
pushes the character
.I c
back on an input stream.
That character
will be returned by the next
.B getc
call on that stream.
.B ungetc
returns
.IR c .
.PP
One character of pushback is guaranteed provided something has been
read from the stream and the stream is actually buffered.
Attempts to
push
.B EOF
are rejected.
.PP
.BR fseek (3)
erases all memory of pushed back characters.
.SH "SEE ALSO"
getc(3), setbuf(3), fseek(3)
.SH DIAGNOSTICS
.B ungetc
returns
.B EOF
if it can't push a character back.
.sp
